{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1381926-how-would-a-sidhe-without-a-house-be-seen","id":1381926,"title":"How would a sidhe without a house be seen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-16T08:30:31-07:00","id":1381926,"title":"How would a sidhe without a house be seen?","content":"We know commoners (probably most) are not members of a house, at least oficially, with a vow. This is not bizarre os unusual. Some houses accept commoners more easily than others, surprisingly house liam is actually pretty hard to get into.<br /> <br /> <br /> But what about sidhes? They are naturally born into a house, or adopted by a house. The sidhe in question could not care one bit about politics and still considered a member of his house. For some it's more than politics anyway. The sidhes are naturally noble by birthright, houses are just another layer to this. Sidhes probably do change houses, either cause they have no memory of past lifes and were adopted by a house after no other house claimed the kithain, or when they actively abandon his house and try to enter another. The later is probably very polemic move that raise eyebrows, but the sidhe still have a house, or the desire to be in one.<br /> <br /> <br /> But what if a sidhe actively refuses to have a house? How would he be seen?<br /> <br /> <br /> My First thought was that he would be seem like a pariah. Even the disgraceful house liam is still a noble house, having no house would be seem like the sidhe is someone that not even the lowly liams would desire (even if the sidhe never tried to enter house liam). Another possibility is that the sidhe would be seem like a dangerous revolutionary/anarchist that rejects his own nobility.<br /> <br /> <br /> How do you think a sidhe without house would be seem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 04-16-2020, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T19:30:18-07:00","id":1382036,"title":"","content":"I imagine it would be akin to real world cases of exiled or cast out nobility. While the nobility might give them greater consideration then they would a commoner, due to the Sidhe's high nature, but they would almost certainly be viewed with suspicion. <br /> <br /> The commoners I imagine would be potentially willing to grant them more consideration then a full titled noble, especially if the Sidhe can prove themselves, but decades of horror and atrocities have rendered many commoners wary of sidhe, although the Autumn Sidhe do have an easier time of that, although they are largely of Houses Liam and Scathach.<br /> <br /> For changelings, nobility is not just a social construct but a genuine law of reality. The Dreaming recognizes the inherent nobility of certain kiths and individuals. This means that those who defy this concept have to radically throw off nobility, such as the Ranters, or those of different political impulses trying to walk their own path.<br /> <br /> Regardless though, nobility is a fact of life for the far. Commoners are inherently common and nobles are inherently noble. Nobles and Commoners who reject these roles are often viewed with suspicion by Changeling society, particularly the community minded Seelie Court.<br /> <br /> Such transgressions are easier to manage so far as the Unseelie Court is concerned. After all 'Change is Good' and 'Honor is a Lie'...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T19:45:08-07:00","id":1382039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1381926-how-would-a-sidhe-without-a-house-be-seen?p=1382036#post1382036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such transgressions are easier to manage so far as the Unseelie Court is concerned. After all 'Change is Good' and 'Honor is a Lie'...</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet they seem to have the more... authortarian Houses(Balor, Ailil, Varich.. Aesin..Dalrean). I would imagine an Unseelie Sidhe with no house would in fact be worse off since there's no base level of acceptance he's fresh meat with no one backing him.<br /> <br /> the Seelie would have at least to play token to the ideas of honor and so on... but still he has no backing. The Commoners who accept nobility are going to see him as an aberration. Those who want to introduce every Noble to Madam Guilotine well here's this noble without any protection. Sure he's CLAIMING to be in it with all you but.. he's not clearly.<br /> <br /> A sidhe without a House needs to be a badass in and of himself that she can survive when there's a target on their back and people shooting from all sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}